ust a  few days after the first movie in this  one john is asked to redeem a so-called  blood oath the mission does not go as  planned and jon is seriously injured  with the help of the bowery king john is  patched up given a weapon and the exact  location of his adversary centino  d'antonio after a tense battle between  john and centino which ends in the  assassin's refuge continental john  forbiddenly shoots the antagonist right  on the spot as a result the mafia  increases the bounty to 14 million  dollars causing john to lose his  privileges and access to the  underworld's resources john wick chapter  3 also picks up directly from his  predecessor and initially shows john on  the run through new york city in search  of the elder of the high table john must  wander through the desert until he can  no longer walk as one of the members  instructs jon eventually finds himself  collapsing from exhaustion in the desert  and indeed he is found there by the  elders henchmen and then brought to him  the elder demands the death of  continental boss winston and so john  makes his way back to new york after  winston betrays him he is shot and falls  from the roof of the hotel john who is  severely injured escapes back to the  bowery king who is neither well disposed  towards the high table after having been  mutilated so much for all the bloody  action until the end of the third film  and all of this is just due to a russian  gangster who had the idea to murder john  wick's dog well that was a huge mistake  the john wick series is known for its  cool and deadly characters so what can  we look forward to in john wick chapter  4. let's take a moment to talk about the  cast of the film and the old as well as  the new characters  first and foremost of course there is  jonathan john wick himself arguably the  world's most popular killer continues to  be played by one of the world's most  popular actors that being keanu reeves  there is nothing but love for the  friendly neighborhood assassin as he did  not start the bloodshed himself but  merely took revenge for his sweet dog  and let's be honest who among us  wouldn't do the same for their  four-legged friend so far he's killed no  less than 306 people in the first three  movies leaving most of the other killers  far behind well maybe with the exception  of marvel's thanos but our anti-hero has  of course not survived entirely  unscathed be it shot stabbed in the  stomach injured by bottles or thrown out  of a building in the end he always  managed to stand up again fix his always  well-fitted suit and look for his next  target  as john's first ex-companion we have to  deal with winston played by ian mcshane  the latter turned on him at the end of  chapter three and shot him several times  until he fell off the continental this  brought the continental back to its old  status and winston back to his old job  whether he intended to kill him or was  aware that he would survive it is not  really clear at the end but after the  adjudicator leaves winston seems to be  smiling and says baba yaga this suggests  that he may know exactly what happened  to jon who just barely survived the fall  and was taken to the bowery king and  this is who we will deal with next the  bowery king is played by lawrence  fishburn which surely put some smiles on  the faces of many matrix fans back then  seeing neo and morpheus face each other  again after such a long time in a  completely different world his real name  is not known and may remain a secret  forever the bowery king compares jon's  injuries to his own and asks him whether  he's angry with the high table after jon  answers in the affirmative he reveals  that he will wage a war against the high  table for wrongfully punishing him and  killing his men jon makes it clear that  he intends to join his war and thus the  groundwork for chapter four is laid a  little side fact the name bowery king is  an allusion to the middle ages  apparently there used to be beggar kings  who got information from vagrants and  homeless people and sold it on similar  to what lord varus did in game of  thrones finally of course we can't do  without lance reddick as chairman he is  the concierge of the hotel in winston's  right-hand man he takes care of all  kinds of tasks in the hotel and also  offers jon all sorts of services for  example taking care of his dog or  shooting people down if he has to  in each part there were also all sorts  of new bounty hunters who were out to  get john this is of course also the case  in john wick 4 thereby we will also see  some faces which we know from other  martial arts movies let's start with the  lesser-known names first we have rina  sawayama in the role of akira sawayama  is mostly known for being a singer and a  model she has made the occasional  appearance on late night shows however  john wick 4 will be her very first film  then scott adkins is best known for many  second-tier action movies and will play  a character named killa here the british  actor and martial artist works not only  as an actor but also as a stunt man  since 1998 he has participated in about  60 productions the most famous among  them should be the expendables 2 doctor  strange and ip man 4. as the third  newcomer we have shamier anderson called  tracker in the film the 31 year old has  been acting in rather small productions  for 10 years therefore the film may also  serve as a stepping stone for him  another martial arts artist signed on is  marco zarror in the role of chidi in  addition to his own acting roles he has  often worked as a stunt double for  dwayne the rock johnson these were the  four less known faces in the movie now  let's move on to the old hands first we  have the young swede bill skarsgard he  will play a character called marquise  his probably biggest role was the clown  pennywise in it there was also part of  marvel's eternals and with hiroyuki  sonata the filmmakers were able to  secure one of the 